  "hints": [
    "Reserving the last units is a race. What makes 'check stock, then reserve' safe?",
    "The rest of the checkout can continue asynchronously as a saga, step by step through a queue.",
    "LB (2) → API (6) with Redis locks (2); API → SQS → orchestrator (2) → DynamoDB; status through Redis."
  ],
  "scoring": {
    "weights": {
      "performance": 0.35,
      "reliability": 0.3,
      "cost": 0.15,
      "architecture": 0.2
    },
    "latencyTargetMs": 40,
    "costBudget": 1288
  },
  "explanation": [
    "Lock (or conditionally update) contended inventory so two buyers can't take the same unit.",
    "Run the checkout as a saga: each step is a local transaction that emits the next step's event; failures trigger compensations in reverse.",
    "Write the order change and its outgoing event in one transaction (the outbox) so nothing is lost between the database and the queue."
  ]
}
